window.DOCS_INDEX = [{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Getting started","url":"index.html#getting-started","text":"Getting started Code karo Hindi mein. JugaadLang uses Roman Hindi keywords, indentation-based blocks, and Python's runtime. This guide takes you from an empty file to a running program."},{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Before you begin","url":"index.html#before-you-begin","text":"Before you begin Install Python 3.10 or newer and JugaadLang using the installation guide . Check your terminal with jug --version ."},{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Your first program","url":"index.html#your-first-program","text":"Your first program Create a UTF-8 file named namaste.jug : naam = \"Duniya\" bolo(\"Namaste, \" + naam + \"!\") Expected output: Namaste, Duniya! Run it from the folder containing the file: jug run namaste.jug bolo prints a value. naam stores a string; you do not need a declaration keyword. A .jug file is a text file containing JugaadLang source."},{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Add a decision","url":"index.html#add-a-decision","text":"Add a decision Blocks start with a colon and use indentation. Use four spaces consistently. chai = 2 agar chai > 0: bolo(\"Chai taiyaar!\") warna: bolo(\"Chai banao.\") Expected output: Chai taiyaar!"},{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Choose your next step","url":"index.html#choose-your-next-step","text":"Choose your next step New to programming? Follow variables , control flow , then the chai bill tutorial . Coming from Python? Read syntax and the keyword mapping . Building something? Explore functions and modules and the standard library . Contributing? Start with the contributor guide and architecture ."},{"title":"Getting started","heading":"Try the interactive shell","url":"index.html#try-the-interactive-shell","text":"Try the interactive shell Run jug repl to experiment without creating a file. Press Enter twice to submit a multiline block. Use Ctrl+C to interrupt input and Ctrl+D to leave the shell. For command options, see the CLI reference . If a command fails, start with debugging ."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Installation and setup","url":"installation.html#installation-and-setup","text":"Installation and setup JugaadLang requires Python 3.10 or newer. Its jug command runs programs, opens the REPL, and provides development tools."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Create an environment","url":"installation.html#create-an-environment","text":"Create an environment Check python --version . On Windows, use py if python is unavailable; on macOS or Linux, use python3 if needed. python -m venv .venv Activate it in your terminal: Terminal Command Windows PowerShell .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1 Windows Command Prompt .venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat macOS / Linux shell source .venv/bin/activate If PowerShell prevents activation, you can use .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe and .venv\\Scripts\\jug.exe directly instead of changing system policy."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Install the language","url":"installation.html#install-the-language","text":"Install the language python -m pip install jugaadlang jug --version jug doctor The version command prints the installed release. jug doctor checks the local environment. Follow getting started to run your first file."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Optional web dependencies","url":"installation.html#optional-web-dependencies","text":"Optional web dependencies For the optional web integrations: python -m pip install \"jugaadlang[web]\" The standard library reference explains the HTTP client and web framework APIs."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Upgrade","url":"installation.html#upgrade","text":"Upgrade python -m pip install --upgrade jugaadlang Use the same Python environment for installation and execution. If jug is not found, activate the environment and check python -m pip show jugaadlang ."},{"title":"Installation","heading":"Editor setup","url":"installation.html#editor-setup","text":"Editor setup Save source files with the .jug extension. The VS Code extension provides language support. A plain text editor and terminal also work. For an editable checkout, tests, and pull requests, see contributing ."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Tutorials and learning paths","url":"tutorials.html#tutorials-and-learning-paths","text":"Tutorials and learning paths Choose a path, then practice by changing a working example."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Beginner path","url":"tutorials.html#beginner-path","text":"Beginner path Install JugaadLang and run your first program . Learn values and collections . Combine expressions with conditions and loops . Extract repeated logic into functions . Complete the chai bill program below and add error handling ."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Coming from Python","url":"tutorials.html#coming-from-python","text":"Coming from Python Read the keyword mapping , syntax reference , and standard library . JugaadLang transpiles to Python, but its parser and available built-ins define which source constructs work; it is not a promise that every Python program runs unchanged."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Build a chai bill","url":"tutorials.html#build-a-chai-bill","text":"Build a chai bill Create chai_bill.jug . The program adds the cost of two orders and applies a discount when the subtotal reaches 100. banao bill(orders, daam): subtotal = 0 ghumo cup mein orders: subtotal += cup * daam agar subtotal >= 100: wapas subtotal - 10 wapas subtotal orders = [2, 3] bolo(\"Total: \" + str(bill(orders, 20))) Run jug run chai_bill.jug . Expected output: Total: 90 The five cups cost 100 before the discount. Try changing the orders to [1, 2] : the total should become 60, with no discount."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Extend it","url":"tutorials.html#extend-it","text":"Extend it Reject negative cup counts with udao ValueError(...) . Store named prices in a dictionary. Write the receipt to a disposable file with the faili module. Add tests for an empty order, a small order, and the exact discount boundary."},{"title":"Tutorials & learning paths","heading":"Contributor path","url":"tutorials.html#contributor-path","text":"Contributor path Read contributing , trace a statement through the architecture , then explore the internal API . Add a small regression test before changing language behavior."},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"JugaadLang Language Specification","url":"syntax.html#jugaadlang-language-specification","text":"JugaadLang Language Specification JugaadLang is a modern programming language with Roman Hindi keywords, transpiled to Python. It mirrors Python's semantic model and block layout while introducing Hindi equivalents for all core keywords, built-in helper functions, funny diagnostics, and micro-frameworks."},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"1. Syntax & Layout","url":"syntax.html#1-syntax-layout","text":"1. Syntax & Layout JugaadLang is an indentation-based language. Code blocks are defined by a colon ( : ) followed by a newline and indent."},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"1.1 Indentation","url":"syntax.html#11-indentation","text":"1.1 Indentation Indentation levels are computed in spaces or tabs (expanded to 8 spaces). Inconsistent indentation (e.g. Mixing spaces and tabs or incorrect dedents) triggers a compiler error."},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"1.2 Comments","url":"syntax.html#12-comments","text":"1.2 Comments JugaadLang supports three comment formats: * # comment \u2014 single-line comment (Python style) * // comment \u2014 single-line comment (C/JS style) * /* comment */ \u2014 multi-line/block comment (C/JS style)"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"2. Keywords","url":"syntax.html#2-keywords","text":"2. Keywords The compiler tokenizes the following keywords: Keyword Python Equivalent Purpose bolo print Output statement poochho input Input statement / expression agar if Conditional branch shayad elif Secondary conditional branch warna else Fallback conditional branch ghumo for Definite loop jabtak while Indefinite loop banao def Function definition wapas return Function return ustad class Class definition khud self Instance self-reference lao import Module import se from Sub-module import rukja break Loop termination chalte_raho continue Loop skip iteration koshish try Exception try block gadbad except Exception catch block aakhir_me finally Exception cleanup block udao raise Exception raise sahi True Boolean true constant galat False Boolean false constant kuch_nahi None Null constant aur and Logical AND operator ya or Logical OR operator nahi not Logical NOT operator tez async Asynchronous modifier intezaar await Asynchronous wait baanto yield Generator yield theek_hai pass Null statement sabka global Global scope variable chota_funkshan lambda Anonymous inline function mein in Membership operator hai is Identity operator"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"3. Data Types","url":"syntax.html#3-data-types","text":"3. Data Types JugaadLang maps natively to Python's dynamic type system: * int : Arbitrary-precision integer (e.g. 10 , 0xFA , 0b101 ) * float : Double-precision floating-point (e.g. 10.5 , 1e-3 ) * str : Unicode string literals (e.g. \"Namaste\" , 'Duniya' , f\"Hi {naam}\" ) * bool : Boolean values ( sahi , galat ) * null : Null value ( kuch_nahi ) * list : Resizable array (e.g. [1, 2, 3] ) * tuple : Immutable array (e.g. (1, 2, 3) ) * dict : Hash table / map (e.g. {\"naam\": \"Sumu\", \"umar\": 20} ) * set : Unique set of elements (e.g. {1, 2, 3} )"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"4. Functions & Classes","url":"syntax.html#4-functions-classes","text":"4. Functions & Classes"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"4.1 Functions (banao)","url":"syntax.html#41-functions-banao","text":"4.1 Functions ( banao ) Functions are declared with banao . They support default arguments, type annotations, and positional/keyword arguments. banao jod(a: int, b: int = 10) -> int: wapas a + b"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"4.2 Classes (ustad)","url":"syntax.html#42-classes-ustad","text":"4.2 Classes ( ustad ) Classes are defined with ustad . The initialization method must be named shuru (which maps to __init__ ). All instance method arguments must specify khud (which maps to self ) as the first argument. ustad Aadmi: banao shuru(khud, naam): khud.naam = naam"},{"title":"Syntax reference","heading":"5. built-in Functions","url":"syntax.html#5-built-in-functions","text":"5. built-in Functions The interpreter automatically injects these interactive functions into the global namespace: * chai() : prints ASCII cup of tea. * himmat() : Prints motivational booster. * ghaas_chhoo() : Prints touch grass advice. * bachao() : Prints emergency help search. * fortune() : Tells a programmer's fortune. * jugaad() : Prints funny debugging tips."},{"title":"Variables & data types","heading":"Variables and data types","url":"variables.html#variables-and-data-types","text":"Variables and data types Assign with = . Names are case-sensitive, and types are determined at runtime. Prefer descriptive names such as kul_daam instead of x ."},{"title":"Variables & data types","heading":"Values","url":"variables.html#values","text":"Values Kind Example Notes Integer umar = 21 Whole numbers Float daam = 12.5 Decimal numbers String naam = \"Asha\" Unicode text Boolean taiyaar = sahi sahi / galat map to Python booleans Empty value result = kuch_nahi Maps to Python None List ank = [10, 20] Ordered, mutable collection Tuple bindu = (2, 3) Ordered, immutable collection Dictionary chai = {\"daam\": 15} Key/value pairs Set alag = {1, 2, 3} Unique values"},{"title":"Variables & data types","heading":"Work with collections","url":"variables.html#work-with-collections","text":"Work with collections Indexes begin at zero. List methods and dictionary access follow Python's model. phal = [\"aam\", \"seb\"] phal.append(\"kela\") bolo(phal[0]) bolo(len(phal)) chai = {\"daam\": 15, \"cup\": 2} bolo(chai[\"daam\"] * chai[\"cup\"]) Expected output: aam 3 30"},{"title":"Variables & data types","heading":"Convert explicitly","url":"variables.html#convert-explicitly","text":"Convert explicitly Input and file contents are text. Use int , float , or str when converting between text and numbers. Invalid numeric text raises ValueError . daam = int(\"25\") bolo(daam + 5) bolo(\"Total: \" + str(daam)) Expected output: 30 Total: 25"},{"title":"Variables & data types","heading":"Mutation and sharing","url":"variables.html#mutation-and-sharing","text":"Mutation and sharing Assigning a list to another variable does not copy it. Both names refer to the same list. Use list(original) for a shallow copy when you need a separate outer collection. Continue with operators , functions and scope , or handling conversion errors ."},{"title":"Operators & expressions","heading":"Operators and expressions","url":"operators.html#operators-and-expressions","text":"Operators and expressions Expressions combine values and produce a result. Use parentheses when they make an expression easier to read."},{"title":"Operators & expressions","heading":"Arithmetic and comparison","url":"operators.html#arithmetic-and-comparison","text":"Arithmetic and comparison Operators Meaning + , - , * , / Addition, subtraction, multiplication, division % , ** Remainder and exponentiation == , != Equal and not equal \u003c , \u003c= , > , >= Ordered comparison = , += , -= Assignment and updating a variable bolo(2 + 3 * 4) bolo((2 + 3) * 4) bolo(7 % 3) bolo(2 ** 3) Expected output: 14 20 1 8 Multiplication binds more tightly than addition. Parentheses change the order. / produces a floating-point result for integer operands."},{"title":"Operators & expressions","heading":"Logic","url":"operators.html#logic","text":"Logic Use aur (and), ya (or), and nahi (not). aur and ya short-circuit, so the second expression is only evaluated when needed. umar = 20 ticket = sahi bolo(umar >= 18 aur ticket) bolo(nahi ticket) bolo(\"aam\" mein [\"seb\", \"aam\"]) Expected output: True False True Printed boolean values use Python's True and False spelling. Use mein for membership, hai for identity, and == for comparing values. The keyword reference also lists mein_nahi and nahi_hai ."},{"title":"Operators & expressions","heading":"Avoid ambiguous intent","url":"operators.html#avoid-ambiguous-intent","text":"Avoid ambiguous intent Use == in a condition, not assignment = . Do not compare strings and numbers without conversion. See variables for conversions and control flow for conditions in programs."},{"title":"Control flow","heading":"Control flow","url":"control-flow.html#control-flow","text":"Control flow Control flow chooses which statements run and how often. Every indented block follows a colon."},{"title":"Control flow","heading":"Make a decision","url":"control-flow.html#make-a-decision","text":"Make a decision ank = 75 agar ank >= 90: bolo(\"Bahut badhiya\") shayad ank >= 60: bolo(\"Pass\") warna: bolo(\"Phir koshish karo\") Expected output: Pass Only the first matching branch runs. shayad and warna are optional."},{"title":"Control flow","heading":"Repeat over a sequence","url":"control-flow.html#repeat-over-a-sequence","text":"Repeat over a sequence ghumo iterates through a collection. range(1, 4) includes 1 and excludes 4. ghumo i mein range(1, 4): bolo(i) Expected output: 1 2 3"},{"title":"Control flow","heading":"Repeat while a condition holds","url":"control-flow.html#repeat-while-a-condition-holds","text":"Repeat while a condition holds Update the condition inside a jabtak loop so it can finish. baaki = 3 jabtak baaki > 0: bolo(baaki) baaki -= 1 Expected output: 3 2 1"},{"title":"Control flow","heading":"Skip or stop","url":"control-flow.html#skip-or-stop","text":"Skip or stop chalte_raho skips the rest of the current iteration. rukja exits the innermost loop. theek_hai is a placeholder statement for a block you will fill in later. ghumo i mein range(5): agar i == 1: chalte_raho agar i == 3: rukja bolo(i) Expected output: 0 2 Next, move repeated logic into functions or build the chai bill tutorial . For exception control flow, see debugging ."},{"title":"Functions & modules","heading":"Functions and modules","url":"functions.html#functions-and-modules","text":"Functions and modules Functions give a name to reusable behavior. Modules group related behavior behind an import."},{"title":"Functions & modules","heading":"Define and call a function","url":"functions.html#define-and-call-a-function","text":"Define and call a function Use banao to define a function and wapas to return a value. Arguments may have defaults. banao kul_daam(cup, daam=15): wapas cup * daam bolo(kul_daam(3)) bolo(kul_daam(2, 20)) Expected output: 45 40 Assignments inside a function normally create local variables. Pass data in and return results instead of relying on global state. Use sabka only when you intentionally need to assign a global name."},{"title":"Functions & modules","heading":"Import a module","url":"functions.html#import-a-module","text":"Import a module Use lao for a module and se ... lao ... for a named import. JugaadLang resolves its standard library names and can import installed Python modules. lao ganit se math lao sqrt bolo(ganit.square(5)) bolo(sqrt(16)) Expected output: 25 4.0 See the standard library for available modules. Third-party Python packages must be installed in the environment used by jug . For module resolution details, consult the architecture ; do not assume a .jug file is automatically importable as a Python module."},{"title":"Functions & modules","heading":"Classes","url":"functions.html#classes","text":"Classes Use ustad to define a class. The constructor is shuru , and khud refers to the instance. ustad Chai: banao shuru(khud, daam): khud.daam = daam banao bill(khud, cup): wapas khud.daam * cup chai = Chai(12) bolo(chai.bill(3)) Expected output: 36 The syntax reference and keyword reference cover annotations, generators, and asynchronous keywords. Start with ordinary functions before introducing those features."},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"JugaadLang Keywords Reference","url":"keywords.html#jugaadlang-keywords-reference","text":"JugaadLang Keywords Reference"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Keyword Mapping","url":"keywords.html#keyword-mapping","text":"Keyword Mapping Every Python keyword has a Hindi (Roman Hindi) equivalent. All keywords are case-sensitive and lowercase."},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Control Flow","url":"keywords.html#control-flow","text":"Control Flow Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example agar if If agar x > 5: bolo(\"bada hai\") shayad elif Maybe/Perhaps shayad x == 5: bolo(\"barabar\") warna else Otherwise warna: bolo(\"chota hai\") ghumo for Roam/Iterate ghumo i mein range(5): jabtak while As long as jabtak x > 0: rukja break Stop! rukja chalte_raho continue Keep going chalte_raho theek_hai pass It's fine theek_hai"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Functions & Classes","url":"keywords.html#functions-classes","text":"Functions & Classes Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example banao def Create/Make banao add(a, b): wapas a + b wapas return Return/Go back wapas result ustad class Master/Teacher ustad Car: khud self Self khud.naam = naam shuru __init__ Start Method name for constructor chota_funkshan lambda Little function chota_funkshan x: x + 1 baanto yield Distribute baanto value"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Exception Handling","url":"keywords.html#exception-handling","text":"Exception Handling Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example koshish try Try/Attempt koshish: gadbad except Problem gadbad ValueError: aakhir_me finally In the end aakhir_me: udao raise Throw udao ValueError(\"kuch gadbad hai\")"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Imports","url":"keywords.html#imports","text":"Imports Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example lao import Bring lao math se from From se math lao sqrt jaise as Like lao numpy jaise np"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Boolean & Operators","url":"keywords.html#boolean-operators","text":"Boolean & Operators Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example sahi True Correct agar sahi: galat False Wrong jabtak galat: kuch_nahi None Nothing x = kuch_nahi aur and And agar x > 0 aur x \u003c 10: ya or Or agar x == 0 ya x == 1: nahi not Not agar nahi x: mein in In ghumo x mein list: mein_nahi not in Not in agar 5 mein_nahi list: hai is Is agar x hai kuch_nahi: nahi_hai is not Is not agar x nahi_hai y:"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Async","url":"keywords.html#async","text":"Async Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example tez async Fast tez banao fetch(): intezaar await Wait intezaar fetch()"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Declarations","url":"keywords.html#declarations","text":"Declarations Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example sabka global Everyone's sabka x gair_local nonlocal Non-local gair_local x pakka assert Guaranteed pakka x > 0, \"positive hona chahiye\" hatao del Remove hatao x ke_saath with With ke_saath open(\"file\") as f:"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Pattern Matching (Python 3.10+)","url":"keywords.html#pattern-matching-python-310","text":"Pattern Matching (Python 3.10+) Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example agar_match match If matches agar_match value: kaand case Case/situation kaand sahi:"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"I/O Keywords","url":"keywords.html#io-keywords","text":"I/O Keywords Keyword Python Equivalent Hindi Meaning Example bolo print Speak bolo(\"Hello\") poochho input Ask poochho naam bulawo (call sugar) Call bulawo func()"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"Built-in Functions (Hindi \u2192 Python Mapping)","url":"keywords.html#built-in-functions-hindi-python-mapping","text":"Built-in Functions (Hindi \u2192 Python Mapping) These JugaadLang built-in function names map directly to Python's built-in functions: JugaadLang Python Meaning maan(x) abs(x) Value sab(x) all(x) All koi_bhi(x) any(x) Any binary(x) bin(x) Binary satyata(x) bool(x) Truth value bulaane_yogya(x) callable(x) Callable akshar(x) chr(x) Character gun_hatao(o, a) delattr(o, a) Remove attribute kosh() dict() Dictionary bhag_shesh(a, b) divmod(a, b) Quotient-remainder ginti(x) enumerate(x) Counting chhano(f, x) filter(f, x) Filter gun_lao(o, a) getattr(o, a) Get attribute gun_hai(o, a) hasattr(o, a) Has attribute madad() help() Help pehchan(x) id(x) Identity purnank(x) int(x) Integer prakar_hai(x, t) isinstance(x, t) Is of type subclass_hai(c, b) issubclass(c, b) Is subclass lambaee(x) len(x) Length suchi(x) list(x) List adhiktam(a, b) max(a, b) Maximum nyuntam(a, b) min(a, b) Minimum agla(x) next(x) Next vastu() object() Object ghat(x, y) pow(x, y) Power ulta(x) reversed(x) Reversed gun_badlo(o, a, v) setattr(o, a, v) Change attribute tukda(a, b, c) slice(a, b, c) Slice kramwar(x) sorted(x) Sequential shabd(x) str(x) Word/string yog(x) sum(x) Sum prakar(x) type(x) Type"},{"title":"Keyword reference","heading":"JugaadLang Built-in Fun Functions","url":"keywords.html#jugaadlang-built-in-fun-functions","text":"JugaadLang Built-in Fun Functions These are custom functions injected at runtime (not in Python stdlib): Function Description chai() \"Chai pi lo\" message himmat() Hidden feature motivation ghaas_chhoo() Touch grass reminder bachao() StackOverflow search fortune() Random programmer fortune jugaad() Random debugging tip nazar() Block bad vibes/bugs ashirwad() Elder blessings dhanya_waad() Gratitude message bhagwan_bhala_kare() Prayer for errors paisa_wasool() Free OSS reminder bas_kar_bhai() Sleep reminder chilla_mat() Calm down reminder kundli() Code horoscope kismat(start, end) Random number sikka() Coin flip (Head/Tail) saaf() Clear terminal ruk(seconds) Sleep/pause bahar() Exit program namaste() Welcome banner debug(var) Debug info version() Show version madad() Full help menu"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"JugaadLang Standard Library Reference","url":"stdlib.html#jugaadlang-standard-library-reference","text":"JugaadLang Standard Library Reference All standard library modules are imported with lao (the Hindi equivalent of import ). Start with functions and modules for import syntax, or installation for optional dependencies. Examples that write files should be run in a disposable working folder."},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"paath \u2014 Text and strings","url":"stdlib.html#paath-text-and-strings","text":"paath \u2014 Text and strings Import with lao paath . Function Behavior ulta(text) Reverse the text palindrome_hai(text) Check a palindrome, ignoring case and spaces shabd_gino(text) Count whitespace-separated words akshar_gino(text) Count characters bada(text) , chota(text) Uppercase or lowercase text title_banao(text) Title-case words saaf(text) Trim leading and trailing whitespace badlo(text, purana, naya) Replace occurrences of a substring shamil_hai(text, khoj) Check whether a substring is present dohrao(text, n) Repeat text n times lao paath bolo(paath.ulta(\"chai\")) bolo(paath.shabd_gino(\"Code karo Hindi mein\")) Expected output: iahc 4"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"1. ganit \u2014 Mathematics","url":"stdlib.html#1-ganit-mathematics","text":"1. ganit \u2014 Mathematics Hindi wrappers for Python's math module. Import: lao ganit"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Constants","url":"stdlib.html#constants","text":"Constants Name Value ganit.pi \u03c0 (3.14159...) ganit.e e (2.71828...) ganit.tau \u03c4 (6.28318...) ganit.inf \u221e ganit.nan NaN"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Trigonometric Functions","url":"stdlib.html#trigonometric-functions","text":"Trigonometric Functions Function Python Equivalent ganit.sin(x) math.sin(x) ganit.cos(x) math.cos(x) ganit.tan(x) math.tan(x) ganit.asin(x) math.asin(x) ganit.acos(x) math.acos(x) ganit.atan(x) math.atan(x) ganit.atan2(y, x) math.atan2(y, x)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Hyperbolic Functions","url":"stdlib.html#hyperbolic-functions","text":"Hyperbolic Functions Function Python Equivalent ganit.sinh(x) math.sinh(x) ganit.cosh(x) math.cosh(x) ganit.tanh(x) math.tanh(x)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Exponential & Logarithmic","url":"stdlib.html#exponential-logarithmic","text":"Exponential & Logarithmic Function Python Equivalent ganit.exp(x) math.exp(x) ganit.log(x) math.log(x) ganit.log10(x) math.log10(x) ganit.log2(x) math.log2(x)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Helpers","url":"stdlib.html#helpers","text":"Helpers Function Python Equivalent ganit.sqrt(x) math.sqrt(x) ganit.ceil(x) math.ceil(x) ganit.floor(x) math.floor(x) ganit.square(x) x * x ganit.cube(x) x * x * x ganit.factorial(x) math.factorial(x) ganit.gcd(a, b) math.gcd(a, b) ganit.degrees(r) math.degrees(r) ganit.radians(d) math.radians(d) ganit.is_nan(x) math.isnan(x) ganit.is_inf(x) math.isinf(x)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example","text":"Example lao ganit bolo(ganit.pi) bolo(ganit.sqrt(16)) bolo(ganit.sin(ganit.pi / 2))"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"2. faili \u2014 File System Operations","url":"stdlib.html#2-faili-file-system-operations","text":"2. faili \u2014 File System Operations Import: lao faili Function Description Python Equivalent faili.padho(path) Read file contents open().read() faili.likho(path, content) Write to file (overwrite) open().write() faili.jodo(path, content) Append to file open().append() faili.mitao(path) Delete file or directory os.remove() / shutil.rmtree() faili.hai_kya(path) Check if path exists os.path.exists() faili.list_karo(path) List directory contents os.listdir() faili.folder_banao(path) Create directory tree os.makedirs()"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_1","text":"Example lao faili faili.likho(\"notes.txt\", \"JugaadLang code likha!\") text = faili.padho(\"notes.txt\") bolo(text) faili.folder_banao(\"myproject/src\")"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"3. json \u2014 JSON Parser","url":"stdlib.html#3-json-json-parser","text":"3. json \u2014 JSON Parser Import: lao json Function Description Python Equivalent json.banao_string(obj, indent) Serialize to JSON string json.dumps() json.banao_object(string) Parse JSON string json.loads() Also re-exports all standard Python json module functions ( load , dump , etc.)."},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_2","text":"Example lao json data = {\"naam\": \"Sumu\", \"umar\": 20} text = json.banao_string(data, indent=2) bolo(text) parsed = json.banao_object(text) bolo(parsed[\"naam\"])"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"4. samay \u2014 Date and Time","url":"stdlib.html#4-samay-date-and-time","text":"4. samay \u2014 Date and Time Import: lao samay Function/Constant Description Python Equivalent samay.samay Current timestamp time.time samay.soja(seconds) Sleep time.sleep() samay.ek_second_rukja() Sleep 1 second time.sleep(1) samay.abhibhi() Current datetime datetime.datetime.now() samay.aaj() Current date datetime.date.today() samay.format_karo(dt, fmt) Format datetime datetime.strftime()"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_3","text":"Example lao samay abhi = samay.abhibhi() bolo(\"Aaj ka time: \" + samay.format_karo(abhi, \"%H:%M:%S\")) aaj_ka_date = samay.aaj() bolo(\"Aaj: \" + str(aaj_ka_date))"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"5. tantra \u2014 System & Environment","url":"stdlib.html#5-tantra-system-environment","text":"5. tantra \u2014 System & Environment Import: lao tantra Name Description Python Equivalent tantra.argv Command-line arguments sys.argv tantra.path Module search path sys.path tantra.platform OS platform name sys.platform tantra.name OS name os.name tantra.pid Process ID os.getpid() tantra.environment Environment variables dict os.environ tantra.exit(code) Exit program sys.exit() tantra.folder_ka_naam() Current working directory os.getcwd() tantra.badlo_folder(path) Change directory os.chdir() tantra.shell_chalao(cmd) Run shell command subprocess.run()"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_4","text":"Example lao tantra bolo(\"OS: \" + tantra.name) bolo(\"Folder: \" + tantra.folder_ka_naam()) bolo(\"Mere arguments: \" + str(tantra.argv))"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"6. crypto \u2014 Cryptography","url":"stdlib.html#6-crypto-cryptography","text":"6. crypto \u2014 Cryptography Import: lao crypto Function Description crypto.sha256(text) SHA-256 hash crypto.md5(text) MD5 hash crypto.base64_encode(text) Base64 encode crypto.base64_decode(text) Base64 decode"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_5","text":"Example lao crypto hash_val = crypto.sha256(\"Namaste Duniya\") bolo(hash_val) encoded = crypto.base64_encode(\"JugaadLang\") bolo(encoded)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"7. database \u2014 JugaadORM (SQLite ORM)","url":"stdlib.html#7-database-jugaadorm-sqlite-orm","text":"7. database \u2014 JugaadORM (SQLite ORM) Import: lao database"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Field Types","url":"stdlib.html#field-types","text":"Field Types Field SQL Type database.String() TEXT database.Integer(primary_key=False) INTEGER database.Float() REAL database.Boolean() INTEGER (0/1)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Model Methods","url":"stdlib.html#model-methods","text":"Model Methods Method Description Model.banao_table() Create SQLite table Model.drop_table() Drop table Model.sab() Fetch all records Model.filter(**kwargs) Filter records instance.bachao() Insert or update record instance.mitao() Delete record"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_6","text":"Example lao database ustad Student(database.Model): naam = database.String() umar = database.Integer() Student.banao_table() st = Student(naam=\"Sumangal\", umar=20) st.bachao() results = Student.filter(naam=\"Sumangal\") ghumo s mein results: bolo(\"Student: \" + s.naam + \", ID: \" + str(s.id))"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"8. web \u2014 HTTP Client & JugaadWeb Framework","url":"stdlib.html#8-web-http-client-jugaadweb-framework","text":"8. web \u2014 HTTP Client & JugaadWeb Framework Import: lao web"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"HTTP Client Functions","url":"stdlib.html#http-client-functions","text":"HTTP Client Functions Function Description Python Equivalent web.get(url) HTTP GET requests.get() web.post(url, data) HTTP POST requests.post() web.put(url, data) HTTP PUT requests.put() web.delete(url) HTTP DELETE requests.delete()"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Global Request State","url":"stdlib.html#global-request-state","text":"Global Request State Name Description web.params Query parameters (during request handling) web.body Request body (during request handling)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"JugaadWeb Framework","url":"stdlib.html#jugaadweb-framework","text":"JugaadWeb Framework Function Description web.agar_route(path, methods=[\"GET\"]) Route decorator web.chalao(port=5000, host=\"127.0.0.1\") Start web server"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"Example","url":"stdlib.html#example_7","text":"Example lao web @web.agar_route(\"/\") banao home(): wapas {\"message\": \"Namaste Duniya!\"} @web.agar_route(\"/data\", [\"GET\", \"POST\"]) banao data(): wapas {\"params\": web.params, \"body\": web.body} web.chalao(port=5001)"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"9. Fun Standard Libraries","url":"stdlib.html#9-fun-standard-libraries","text":"9. Fun Standard Libraries"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"chai \u2014 Tea Module","url":"stdlib.html#chai-tea-module","text":"chai \u2014 Tea Module Import: lao chai - chai.piyo() \u2014 Print ASCII tea art - chai.status() \u2014 Return chai status string"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"jokes \u2014 Programmer Jokes","url":"stdlib.html#jokes-programmer-jokes","text":"jokes \u2014 Programmer Jokes Import: lao jokes - jokes.sunao() \u2014 Print random programmer joke"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"motivation \u2014 Motivation Quotes","url":"stdlib.html#motivation-motivation-quotes","text":"motivation \u2014 Motivation Quotes Import: lao motivation - motivation.gyan() \u2014 Print random motivational quote"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"fortune \u2014 Fortune Telling","url":"stdlib.html#fortune-fortune-telling","text":"fortune \u2014 Fortune Telling Import: lao fortune - fortune.batao() \u2014 Print random developer fortune"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"memes \u2014 ASCII Memes","url":"stdlib.html#memes-ascii-memes","text":"memes \u2014 ASCII Memes Import: lao memes - memes.dikhao() \u2014 Print random ASCII art meme"},{"title":"Standard library","heading":"catfacts \u2014 Cat Facts","url":"stdlib.html#catfacts-cat-facts","text":"catfacts \u2014 Cat Facts Import: lao catfacts - catfacts.batao() \u2014 Print random cat fact"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"JugaadLang CLI Reference","url":"cli.html#jugaadlang-cli-reference","text":"JugaadLang CLI Reference"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"Usage","url":"cli.html#usage","text":"Usage jug [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]..."},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"Global Options","url":"cli.html#global-options","text":"Global Options Option Description --version Show version and exit --help Show help message and exit"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"Commands","url":"cli.html#commands","text":"Commands"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug run FILE [ARGS...]","url":"cli.html#jug-run-file-args","text":"jug run FILE [ARGS...] Run a JugaadLang .jug file. File : Path to a .jug file (other extensions work with a warning) ARGS : Additional arguments passed to the script (accessible via tantra.argv ) jug run main.jug jug run main.jug arg1 arg2"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug repl","url":"cli.html#jug-repl","text":"jug repl Start the interactive JugaadLang REPL (Read-Eval-Print Loop). Syntax highlighting via Pygments Auto-completion for all keywords History persistence ( ~/.jugaadlang/repl_history.txt ) Double-Enter to execute multi-line blocks jug repl"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug install PACKAGE","url":"cli.html#jug-install-package","text":"jug install PACKAGE Install a package or custom bundle. PACKAGE : PyPI package name or bundle alias Alias Installs web flask, requests, httpx, aiohttp dev pytest, pytest-cov, black, mypy, ruff ml numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib * Any PyPI package (passthrough) jug install web jug install flask"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug remove PACKAGE","url":"cli.html#jug-remove-package","text":"jug remove PACKAGE Uninstall a package or bundle. jug remove web"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug update PACKAGE","url":"cli.html#jug-update-package","text":"jug update PACKAGE Update a package or bundle to the latest version. jug update web"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug search QUERY","url":"cli.html#jug-search-query","text":"jug search QUERY Search for packages in PyPI and JugaadLang standard library. jug search chai jug search requests"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug new PROJECT_NAME","url":"cli.html#jug-new-project_name","text":"jug new PROJECT_NAME Create a new JugaadLang project boilerplate. jug new my_project Creates: my_project/ \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.jug # Boilerplate .jug file \u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md # Project README"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug compile FILE -o OUTPUT","url":"cli.html#jug-compile-file-o-output","text":"jug compile FILE -o OUTPUT Transpile a JugaadLang .jug file to equivalent Python source code. -o, --output FILE : Write output to a file (otherwise prints to stdout) jug compile main.jug -o main.py jug compile main.jug # prints Python source to stdout"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug check FILE","url":"cli.html#jug-check-file","text":"jug check FILE Validate a JugaadLang file's syntax without executing it. jug check main.jug"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug typecheck FILE","url":"cli.html#jug-typecheck-file","text":"jug typecheck FILE Type-check a JugaadLang file using mypy (behind the scenes). jug typecheck main.jug"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"jug doctor","url":"cli.html#jug-doctor","text":"jug doctor Diagnose the JugaadLang installation (Python version, core imports, and optional extras). jug doctor"},{"title":"Command-line tools","heading":"Examples","url":"cli.html#examples","text":"Examples # Run a file jug run hello.jug # Start REPL jug repl # Install a bundle jug install web # Create a new project jug new myapp # Transpile to Python jug compile myapp/main.jug -o myapp/main.py # Check syntax jug check myapp/main.jug"},{"title":"Errors & debugging","heading":"Error handling and debugging","url":"debugging.html#error-handling-and-debugging","text":"Error handling and debugging JugaadLang reports errors with Hindi diagnostics. Read the exception type, filename, and line information along with the friendly message."},{"title":"Errors & debugging","heading":"Catch an expected failure","url":"debugging.html#catch-an-expected-failure","text":"Catch an expected failure koshish , gadbad , and aakhir_me correspond to try, except, and finally. Catch a specific exception you know how to handle. koshish: ank = int(\"chai\") gadbad ValueError: bolo(\"Number likho.\") aakhir_me: bolo(\"Jaanch poori.\") Expected output: Number likho. Jaanch poori. Use udao ValueError(\"message\") to reject an invalid value in your own code. A wapas inside a function can return a successful result; an exception communicates a failure the caller must handle."},{"title":"Errors & debugging","heading":"Common problems","url":"debugging.html#common-problems","text":"Common problems Error Check Syntax or indentation error Missing colon, unmatched bracket, or inconsistent spaces NameError Spelling and whether the name was assigned before use TypeError Text versus numbers; argument count and types IndexError List size and zero-based indexes KeyError Whether the dictionary contains the key ModuleNotFoundError Import spelling and the active Python environment ZeroDivisionError Validate the denominator before dividing"},{"title":"Errors & debugging","heading":"A debugging workflow","url":"debugging.html#a-debugging-workflow","text":"A debugging workflow Reduce the program to the smallest input that still fails. Run jug check main.jug to check syntax without executing it. Print intermediate values with bolo . Run jug compile main.jug -o main.py to inspect the generated Python source. Use jug typecheck main.jug for optional static checks; this command uses mypy and may require installing it. Compilation and syntax checks do not prove runtime correctness. Exercise normal inputs, boundary values, and invalid inputs. See the CLI reference and coding guidelines ."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Best practices","url":"practices.html#best-practices","text":"Best practices Readable JugaadLang uses familiar Hindi keywords with clear names and predictable structure."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Make code easy to follow","url":"practices.html#make-code-easy-to-follow","text":"Make code easy to follow Use four spaces per indentation level and avoid mixing tabs and spaces. Use snake_case for variables and functions, and descriptive class names. Keep functions focused on one task. Prefer parameters and return values to global state. Explain why a decision exists in comments; avoid repeating what the next line does. Use parentheses to make complex boolean conditions unambiguous."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Validate boundaries","url":"practices.html#validate-boundaries","text":"Validate boundaries Convert input explicitly and catch the specific conversion error. Validate file paths, collection indexes, and external data before using them. Do not silently catch every exception: unexpected failures should remain visible while debugging."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Make examples reproducible","url":"practices.html#make-examples-reproducible","text":"Make examples reproducible Show input and expected output. Keep beginner examples independent of network services, randomness, local credentials, and existing files. Create disposable files in a dedicated example folder when teaching file operations."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Organize a project","url":"practices.html#organize-a-project","text":"Organize a project Start with jug new my_project . Keep source, tests, and supporting data clearly separated. Use a virtual environment and record Python dependencies. Keep credentials out of source files and Git history."},{"title":"Coding guidelines","heading":"Before sharing","url":"practices.html#before-sharing","text":"Before sharing Run syntax checks, exercise the program with representative inputs, and document the command needed to run it. Contributors should also run the repository's checks in the contributor guide . Related: functions and modules , debugging , and the tutorial ."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Frequently asked questions","url":"faq.html#frequently-asked-questions","text":"Frequently asked questions"},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Do I need to know Hindi?","url":"faq.html#do-i-need-to-know-hindi","text":"Do I need to know Hindi? No. Keywords use Roman Hindi, and the keyword reference pairs them with Python equivalents. The guides explain each keyword as it is introduced."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Do I need Python installed?","url":"faq.html#do-i-need-python-installed","text":"Do I need Python installed? Yes. JugaadLang requires Python 3.10 or newer and executes compiled code through Python. Follow installation to keep it in a virtual environment."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Why does a boolean print as True or False?","url":"faq.html#why-does-a-boolean-print-as-true-or-false","text":"Why does a boolean print as True or False? sahi and galat map to Python boolean values. Printing them uses Python's spelling. kuch_nahi similarly maps to None ."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Why is jug not found after installation?","url":"faq.html#why-is-jug-not-found-after-installation","text":"Why is jug not found after installation? The command may belong to a different environment. Activate the environment where you installed the package and run python -m pip show jugaadlang . On Windows you can invoke .venv\\Scripts\\jug.exe directly."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Can I use Python libraries?","url":"faq.html#can-i-use-python-libraries","text":"Can I use Python libraries? Installed Python modules can be imported with lao or se ... lao ... . Install packages into the same environment as JugaadLang. See functions and modules and the CLI reference ."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Is this a browser playground?","url":"faq.html#is-this-a-browser-playground","text":"Is this a browser playground? This documentation explains how to run programs locally. Code blocks are examples, not an in-browser interpreter. Use jug run or jug repl to execute them."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"Where should I report a bug?","url":"faq.html#where-should-i-report-a-bug","text":"Where should I report a bug? Open an issue with your JugaadLang and Python versions, the smallest reproducing program, expected behavior, and actual output. For security reports, follow the repository's security policy ."},{"title":"FAQ","heading":"How can I improve these docs?","url":"faq.html#how-can-i-improve-these-docs","text":"How can I improve these docs? Use the \u201cEdit this page\u201d link on any article. The portal is generated from Markdown; the contributor guide explains how to build and check it locally."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Contributing to JugaadLang","url":"contributing.html#contributing-to-jugaadlang","text":"Contributing to JugaadLang First time? Read CONTRIBUTING.md at the project root for the quick-start guide. This document provides deeper technical guidance for contributors."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Development Setup","url":"contributing.html#development-setup","text":"Development Setup"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Prerequisites","url":"contributing.html#prerequisites","text":"Prerequisites Python 3.10 or later pip, uv, or your preferred Python package manager"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Installation","url":"contributing.html#installation","text":"Installation # Clone your fork git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/jugaadlang.git cd jugaadlang # Editable install with all extras pip install -e .[dev,all] # Or with uv uv sync --dev"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Verify Setup","url":"contributing.html#verify-setup","text":"Verify Setup jug --version jug run examples/01_namaste_duniya.jug jug repl"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Project Architecture","url":"contributing.html#project-architecture","text":"Project Architecture See docs/architecture.md for detailed architecture documentation."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Quick Overview","url":"contributing.html#quick-overview","text":"Quick Overview Source (.jug) \u2192 Lexer (tokens) \u2192 Parser (JL AST) \u2192 Transformer (Python AST) \u2192 compile() (bytecode) \u2192 exec() (execute)"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Key Modules","url":"contributing.html#key-modules","text":"Key Modules Module Purpose jugaadlang/lexer/ Tokenizer with indentation tracking jugaadlang/ast_nodes/ AST node definitions (dataclasses) jugaadlang/parser/ Recursive-descent parser jugaadlang/transformer/ JL AST \u2192 Python AST converter jugaadlang/runtime/ Execution engine + built-in functions jugaadlang/errors/ Funny Hindi error formatter jugaadlang/stdlib/ Standard library modules jugaadlang/package_manager/ Package manager (pip wrapper) jugaadlang/repl/ Interactive REPL jug_cli/ Command-line interface"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Coding Standards","url":"contributing.html#coding-standards","text":"Coding Standards"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Code Style","url":"contributing.html#code-style","text":"Code Style Line length : 100 characters Formatter : ruff (replaces black/isort/flake8) Type hints : Required for all function signatures ( from __future__ import annotations ) Docstrings : Required for public modules, classes, and functions"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Running the Formatter","url":"contributing.html#running-the-formatter","text":"Running the Formatter ruff check . ruff check --fix ."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Running Type Checks","url":"contributing.html#running-type-checks","text":"Running Type Checks mypy jugaadlang/ jug_cli/"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Running Tests","url":"contributing.html#running-tests","text":"Running Tests pytest pytest -v # verbose pytest --cov # with coverage pytest tests/test_lexer.py # single test file"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Test Structure","url":"contributing.html#test-structure","text":"Test Structure Tests are in the tests/ directory using pytest : File Tests tests/test_lexer.py Lexer tokenization tests/test_parser.py Parser AST generation tests/test_runtime.py Full execution pipeline tests/test_errors.py Error formatting"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Adding a New Keyword","url":"contributing.html#adding-a-new-keyword","text":"Adding a New Keyword Token type : Add to TokenType enum in jugaadlang/lexer/tokens.py Keyword mapping : Add to KEYWORDS dict in jugaadlang/lexer/tokens.py Lexer : Ensure the lexer tokenizes the keyword (should work automatically via _scan_identifier ) AST node : If a new statement/expression type, add node class in jugaadlang/ast_nodes/nodes.py Parser : Add parse method in jugaadlang/parser/parser.py and dispatch in parse_statement() or parse_expression() Transformer : Add visit_{NodeType} method in jugaadlang/transformer/to_python.py Built-in mapping : If a built-in function, add to globals dict in jugaadlang/runtime/interpreter.py REPL : Add to KEYWORDS_LIST in jugaadlang/repl/repl.py for auto-completion Pygments lexer : Add to JugaadPygmentsLexer in jugaadlang/repl/repl.py for syntax highlighting Tests : Add test cases in the appropriate test file Docs : Update docs/keywords.md and docs/spec.md"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Adding a Standard Library Module","url":"contributing.html#adding-a-standard-library-module","text":"Adding a Standard Library Module Create a new .py file in jugaadlang/stdlib/ Import and register it in jugaadlang/stdlib/__init__.py Add to the local_stdlibs list in jugaadlang/package_manager/manager.py for search support Add tests for the module Document in docs/stdlib.md"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Release Process","url":"contributing.html#release-process","text":"Release Process"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Version Bumping","url":"contributing.html#version-bumping","text":"Version Bumping Version is defined in two places: - pyproject.toml \u2192 [project] version - jugaadlang/__init__.py \u2192 __version__ Update both using: ./update_version.sh 1.1.1"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Building","url":"contributing.html#building","text":"Building python -m build Creates dist/jugaadlang-{version}.tar.gz and dist/jugaadlang-{version}-py3-none-any.whl ."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Publishing to PyPI","url":"contributing.html#publishing-to-pypi","text":"Publishing to PyPI twine check dist/* twine upload dist/*"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Creating a GitHub Release","url":"contributing.html#creating-a-github-release","text":"Creating a GitHub Release Tag the release: git tag v1.1.1 Push tags: git push --tags Create a release on GitHub \u2192 triggers automated release.yml workflow"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Pull Request Guidelines","url":"contributing.html#pull-request-guidelines","text":"Pull Request Guidelines Branch from main with a descriptive name (e.g., feature/pattern-matching , fix/parser-error ) Keep PRs focused on a single concern Include tests for new features and bug fixes Ensure CI passes (runs tests on Python 3.10\u20133.14 + ruff linting) Update documentation if changing behavior or adding features Write meaningful commit messages"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Commit Message Format","url":"contributing.html#commit-message-format","text":"Commit Message Format \u003ctype>: \u003cshort description> \u003coptional body> Types: feat: , fix: , docs: , test: , refactor: , style: , chore: , ci: Example: feat: add kismat() built-in for random number generation"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Debugging Tips","url":"contributing.html#debugging-tips","text":"Debugging Tips Use jug check file.jug to validate syntax without execution Use jug compile file.jug to see the transpiled Python output Use debug(variable) inside JugaadLang code to inspect values Set PYTHONDEVMODE=1 for extra Python runtime checks"},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Working on the documentation website","url":"contributing.html#working-on-the-documentation-website","text":"Working on the documentation website The documentation portal is a static site at website/docs/ . Its HTML and search index are generated from the Markdown files in docs/ and docs/guides/ . Navigation and page order are defined in scripts/build_docs.py ; the shared layout lives in docs/site/template.html . Styles and browser behavior live in website/docs/docs.css , theme.js , and docs.js . Install the build dependency and regenerate after editing Markdown or the template: python -m pip install -e \".[dev]\" -r docs/requirements.txt python scripts/build_docs.py python scripts/build_docs.py --check python -m pytest tests/test_documentation.py python -m http.server 8000 --directory website Open http://localhost:8000/docs/ . Commit the generated HTML and search index along with source changes, so existing static hosting can serve the portal without a build step. CI checks that generated files match their sources. Do not edit generated HTML directly. Guide code blocks marked jugaadlang followed by an expected text output block are executed in the documentation tests. Keep these examples deterministic and independent of network access. Check navigation, search, copy buttons, keyboard access, light/dark themes, and narrow screens when changing the portal UI. Related: architecture , internal API , and coding guidelines ."},{"title":"Contributor guide","heading":"Getting Help","url":"contributing.html#getting-help","text":"Getting Help Issues : https://github.com/JugaadLang/jugaadlang/issues Discussions : GitHub Discussions page Email : jugaadlang@atomicmail.io"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"JugaadLang Architecture","url":"architecture.html#jugaadlang-architecture","text":"JugaadLang Architecture"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"Overview","url":"architecture.html#overview","text":"Overview JugaadLang is a Hindi-keyword programming language that transforms its own syntax tree into Python AST (Abstract Syntax Tree), compiles it to bytecode, and executes it on the Python VM. Parsing, transformation, and runtime helpers have costs; this is not a zero-overhead guarantee. The runtime caches generated Python source to reuse it on subsequent executions."},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"Pipeline","url":"architecture.html#pipeline","text":"Pipeline Source (.jug) \u2502 \u25bc \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u2502 Lexer \u2502 Tokenizes source into tokens (jugaadlang/lexer/lexer.py) \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2502 tokens \u25bc \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u2502 Parser \u2502 Recursive-descent parser \u2192 JugaadLang AST (jugaadlang/parser/parser.py) \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2502 JL AST \u25bc \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u2502 Transformer \u2502 Converts JL AST \u2192 Python AST (jugaadlang/transformer/to_python.py) \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2502 Python AST \u25bc \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u2502 compile() \u2502 Python's built-in: Python AST \u2192 bytecode \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2502 bytecode \u25bc \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u2502 exec() \u2502 Python VM executes bytecode \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"Directory Structure","url":"architecture.html#directory-structure","text":"Directory Structure jugaadlang/ \u251c\u2500\u2500 jug_cli/ # Command-line interface \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.py # Click-based CLI entry point \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 jugaadlang/ # Core language implementation \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 ast_nodes/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 nodes.py # JugaadLang AST node definitions (dataclasses) \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 errors/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 messages.py # Funny Hindi error formatting \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 lexer/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 lexer.py # Source tokenizer with indentation tracking \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 tokens.py # TokenType enum and keyword mapping \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 parser/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 parser.py # Recursive-descent parser \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 runtime/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 interpreter.py # Execution harness, built-in functions \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 transformer/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 to_python.py # JL AST \u2192 Python AST visitor \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 stdlib/ # Standard library modules (importable via `lao`) \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 ganit.py # Mathematics \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 web.py # HTTP client + JugaadWeb framework \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 faili.py # File system \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 json.py # JSON parser \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 samay.py # Date/time \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 tantra.py # System/environment \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 crypto.py # Hashing & encoding \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 database.py # JugaadORM (SQLite ORM) \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 chai.py # Tea-themed utility \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 jokes.py # Programmer jokes \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 motivation.py # Motivational quotes \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 fortune.py # Fortune telling \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 memes.py # ASCII art memes \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 catfacts.py # Cat facts \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 REPL/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 repl.py # Interactive REPL with syntax highlighting \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 package_manager/ \u2502 \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 manager.py # Package installation/search/removal \u2502 \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py # Version info \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml # Project metadata & dependencies \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/ \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_lexer.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_parser.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_runtime.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_errors.py \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 __init__.py \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 docs/ \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 spec.md # Language specification \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 architecture.md # This file \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 grammar.ebnf # Formal EBNF grammar \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 keywords.md # Keyword reference \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 stdlib.md # Standard library reference \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.md # CLI command reference \u2502 \u2514\u2500\u2500 api.md # Internal API reference \u2502 \u251c\u2500\u2500 examples/ # Example .jug programs \u251c\u2500\u2500 scratch/ # Scratch/test files \u251c\u2500\u2500 website/ # Landing page HTML/CSS \u251c\u2500\u2500 vscode_extension/ # VS Code syntax highlighting extension \u2514\u2500\u2500 docker/ # Docker deployment files"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"Core Components","url":"architecture.html#core-components","text":"Core Components"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"1. Lexer (jugaadlang/lexer/)","url":"architecture.html#1-lexer-jugaadlanglexer","text":"1. Lexer ( jugaadlang/lexer/ ) The lexer tokenizes raw source code into a stream of Token objects. Key features: Indentation tracking : Implements Python-style INDENT/DEDENT tokens using a stack-based approach Multi-line comments : Supports # , // , and /* */ comment styles String literals : Single, double, triple-quoted, and f-strings Number literals : Decimal, hex ( 0x ), octal ( 0o ), binary ( 0b ), floats with exponents Unicode identifiers : Full Unicode + emoji support in identifiers"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"2. Parser (jugaadlang/parser/)","url":"architecture.html#2-parser-jugaadlangparser","text":"2. Parser ( jugaadlang/parser/ ) A recursive-descent parser with precedence climbing for expressions. Produces a JugaadLang-specific AST (defined in jugaadlang/ast_nodes/nodes.py ). Supports all Python control flow: if / elif / else , for , while , try / except / finally Full pattern matching ( agar_match / kaand ) translating to Python 3.10+ match / case Comprehensions (list, dict, set, generator) Async/await, generator yield Decorators, type annotations Walrus operator ( := )"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"3. Transformer (jugaadlang/transformer/to_python.py)","url":"architecture.html#3-transformer-jugaadlangtransformerto_pythonpy","text":"3. Transformer ( jugaadlang/transformer/to_python.py ) The transformer walks the JugaadLang AST and emits corresponding Python AST nodes. This is where keywords are mapped: bolo \u2192 print agar \u2192 if shuru (method name) \u2192 __init__ khud \u2192 self All Hindi built-in names \u2192 Python built-in names"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"4. Interpreter (jugaadlang/runtime/interpreter.py)","url":"architecture.html#4-interpreter-jugaadlangruntimeinterpreterpy","text":"4. Interpreter ( jugaadlang/runtime/interpreter.py ) The interpreter orchestrates the full pipeline: Lex \u2192 Parse \u2192 Transform \u2192 Compile \u2192 Execute Maintains a persistent global namespace (shared across REPL sessions) Injects built-in functions ( chai , fortune , jugaad , etc.) and built-in name mappings ( maan \u2192 abs , lambaee \u2192 len , etc.) Error handling with funny Hindi diagnostic messages"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"5. Error System (jugaadlang/errors/messages.py)","url":"architecture.html#5-error-system-jugaadlangerrorsmessagespy","text":"5. Error System ( jugaadlang/errors/messages.py ) Errors are caught at the runtime level and re-formatted with humorous Hindi messages: Error Type Title SyntaxError \ud83e\udd26 Bhai kya likh diya? NameError \ud83d\udd75\ufe0f Variable '...' dhundte dhundte thak gaya. ZeroDivisionError \ud83d\udc80 Zero se divide? TypeError \ud83e\udd14 Type mismatch ho gaya. IndexError \ud83d\udced List mein itna nahi hai! KeyError \ud83d\udd11 Key gayab hai! AttributeError \ud83d\udeab Attribute mila hi nahi."},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"6. CLI (jug_cli/main.py)","url":"architecture.html#6-cli-jug_climainpy","text":"6. CLI ( jug_cli/main.py ) Built with Click and Rich . Commands: run , repl , install , remove , update , search , new , compile , check , typecheck , doctor ."},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"7. REPL (jugaadlang/repl/repl.py)","url":"architecture.html#7-repl-jugaadlangreplreplpy","text":"7. REPL ( jugaadlang/repl/repl.py ) Interactive shell using prompt_toolkit with: - Syntax highlighting (via custom Pygments lexer) - Auto-completion for all keywords and built-ins - Auto-suggest from history - Multi-line block input (double-Enter to execute)"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"8. Package Manager (jugaadlang/package_manager/manager.py)","url":"architecture.html#8-package-manager-jugaadlangpackage_managermanagerpy","text":"8. Package Manager ( jugaadlang/package_manager/manager.py ) Wraps pip with JugaadLang-specific bundle aliases: Alias Packages web flask, requests, httpx, aiohttp dev pytest, pytest-cov, black, mypy, ruff ml numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib * Any PyPI package passthrough"},{"title":"Architecture","heading":"Translation Examples","url":"architecture.html#translation-examples","text":"Translation Examples JugaadLang Python (after transpilation) bolo(\"Namaste\") print(\"Namaste\") agar x > 5: if x > 5: ghumo i mein range(10): for i in range(10): banao jod(a, b): wapas a + b def jod(a, b): return a + b ustad Animal: class Animal: banao shuru(khud, naam): def __init__(self, naam): koshish: ... gadbad: ... try: ... except: ... tez banao fetch(): async def fetch(): intezaar result await result poochho naam naam = input() lao ganit import ganit se math lao sqrt from math import sqrt"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"JugaadLang Internal API Reference","url":"api.html#jugaadlang-internal-api-reference","text":"JugaadLang Internal API Reference"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Package: jugaadlang","url":"api.html#package-jugaadlang","text":"Package: jugaadlang"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang/__init__.py","url":"api.html#jugaadlang__init__py","text":"jugaadlang/__init__.py from jugaadlang import __version__ __author__ = \"JugaadLang Community\" __license__ = \"MIT\""},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.lexer","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlanglexer","text":"Module: jugaadlang.lexer"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.lexer.tokens","url":"api.html#jugaadlanglexertokens","text":"jugaadlang.lexer.tokens class TokenType(Enum) All token types used by the lexer. Categories: - Literals : INT , FLOAT , STRING , FSTRING - Keywords : BOLO , POOCHHO , AGAR , SHAYAD , WARNA , GHUMO , JABTAK , BANAO , WAPAS , USTAD , KHUD , LAO , SE , RUKJA , CHALTE_RAHO , KOSHISH , GADBAD , AAKHIR_ME , UDAO , SAHI , GALAT , KUCH_NAHI , AUR , YA , NAHI , TEZ , INTEZAAR , BAANTO , THEEK_HAI , SABKA , CHOTA_FUNKSHAN , MEIN , MEIN_NAHI , HAI , NAHI_HAI , BULAWO , DEL , NONLOCAL , WITH , AS , ASSERT , AGAR_MATCH , KAAND - Operators : PLUS , MINUS , STAR , SLASH , DOUBLESLASH , PERCENT , DOUBLESTAR , EQ , NEQ , LT , GT , LTE , GTE , ASSIGN , PLUS_ASSIGN , MINUS_ASSIGN , STAR_ASSIGN , SLASH_ASSIGN , PERCENT_ASSIGN , DOUBLESTAR_ASSIGN , DOUBLESLASH_ASSIGN , ARROW , WALRUS , AT , AT_ASSIGN , TILDE , AMP , PIPE , CARET , LSHIFT , RSHIFT , AMP_ASSIGN , PIPE_ASSIGN , CARET_ASSIGN , LSHIFT_ASSIGN , RSHIFT_ASSIGN - Delimiters : LPAREN , RPAREN , LBRACKET , RBRACKET , LBRACE , RBRACE , COMMA , DOT , COLON , SEMICOLON , ELLIPSIS - Layout : NEWLINE , INDENT , DEDENT - Special : COMMENT , EOF KEYWORDS: dict[str, TokenType] Maps keyword strings to their TokenType . Includes bilingual support: - \"hatao\" \u2192 TokenType.DEL (alternative for del ) - \"gair_local\" \u2192 TokenType.NONLOCAL (alternative for nonlocal ) - \"ke_saath\" \u2192 TokenType.WITH (alternative for with ) - \"jaise\" \u2192 TokenType.AS (alternative for as ) - \"pakka\" \u2192 TokenType.ASSERT (alternative for assert ) @dataclass class Token Field Type Description type TokenType The token type value str The token's string value line int Source line number col int Source column number Methods: is_keyword() -> bool"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.lexer.lexer","url":"api.html#jugaadlanglexerlexer","text":"jugaadlang.lexer.lexer class Lexer Method Returns Description Lexer(source, filename) \u2014 Initialize with source string and optional filename .tokenize() list[Token] Tokenize the entire source Internal: Uses INDENT/DEDENT stack for indentation-based block detection. Supports # , // , /* */ comments, all string types (single, double, triple, f-strings), and all number formats."},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.ast_nodes","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangast_nodes","text":"Module: jugaadlang.ast_nodes"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.ast_nodes.nodes","url":"api.html#jugaadlangast_nodesnodes","text":"jugaadlang.ast_nodes.nodes All AST nodes are @dataclass inheriting from ASTNode (base), Stmt , or Expr . Statements: Module , FunctionDef , ClassDef , Return , Delete , Assign , AugAssign , AnnAssign , For , While , If , With , Raise , Try , Assert , Import , ImportFrom , Global , Nonlocal , ExprStmt , Pass , Break , Continue , PoochhoStmt , Match Expressions: BoolOp , BinOp , UnaryOp , Lambda , IfExp , Dict , Set , ListComp , SetComp , DictComp , GeneratorExp , Await , Yield , YieldFrom , Compare , Call , FormattedValue , JoinedStr , Constant , Attribute , Subscript , Starred , Name , List , Tuple , Slice Helper Nodes: arg , arguments , keyword , alias , withitem , ExceptHandler , comprehension Pattern Matching Nodes: Match , match_case , MatchValue , MatchSingleton , MatchAs , MatchOr , MatchSequence , MatchMapping , MatchClass Each node includes line: int and col: int fields for error reporting."},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.parser","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangparser","text":"Module: jugaadlang.parser"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.parser.parser","url":"api.html#jugaadlangparserparser","text":"jugaadlang.parser.parser class Parser Method Returns Description Parser(tokens, filename, source) \u2014 Initialize with token list .parse() Module Parse the entire token stream into an AST Internal recursive-descent parser with these parse methods: - .parse_statement() \u2014 Top-level statement dispatcher - .parse_expression() \u2014 Expression entry (precedence climbing) - .parse_block() \u2014 Indented block or inline statement - .parse_function_def(is_async) \u2014 banao / tez banao - .parse_class_def() \u2014 ustad - .parse_if() / .parse_elif() \u2014 agar / shayad / warna - .parse_for(is_async) \u2014 ghumo / tez ghumo - .parse_while() \u2014 jabtak - .parse_match() \u2014 agar_match / kaand - .parse_try() \u2014 koshish / gadbad / aakhir_me - .parse_lambda() \u2014 chota_funkshan - .parse_import() / .parse_import_from() \u2014 lao / se ... lao"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.transformer","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangtransformer","text":"Module: jugaadlang.transformer"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.transformer.to_python","url":"api.html#jugaadlangtransformerto_python","text":"jugaadlang.transformer.to_python class JugaadToPythonTransformer Method Returns Description JugaadToPythonTransformer(filename) \u2014 Initialize transformer .transform(node: Module) ast.Module Transform entire JL AST to Python AST .visit(node, ctx) ast.AST Dispatch visitor by node type Each visit_{NodeType} method handles a specific JL AST node and returns the corresponding Python AST node. Key translations: - shuru \u2192 __init__ - khud \u2192 self - bolo \u2192 print - poochho \u2192 input - All Hindi built-in names \u2192 Python built-in names (mapped in visit_Name )"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.runtime","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangruntime","text":"Module: jugaadlang.runtime"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.runtime.interpreter","url":"api.html#jugaadlangruntimeinterpreter","text":"jugaadlang.runtime.interpreter class JugaadInterpreter Method Returns Description JugaadInterpreter(filename) \u2014 Init with persistent global namespace .run(source) None Execute JugaadLang source (exec mode) .run_expression(source) Any Evaluate expression (eval mode) or execute statements The interpreter maintains a globals dict that persists across calls (important for REPL). Built-in Functions (injected at interpreter init): Group Functions Standard I/O bolo \u2192 print , poochho \u2192 input Random kismat(start, end) , sikka() System saaf() , ruk(seconds) , bahar() Fun namaste() , chai() , himmat() , ghaas_chhoo() , bachao() , fortune() , jugaad() , nazar() , ashirwad() , dhanya_waad() , bhagwan_bhala_kare() , paisa_wasool() , bas_kar_bhai() , chilla_mat() , kundli() Dev debug(var) , version() , madad() Built-in Mappings maan \u2192 abs , sab \u2192 all , lambaee \u2192 len , etc."},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.errors","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangerrors","text":"Module: jugaadlang.errors"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.errors.messages","url":"api.html#jugaadlangerrorsmessages","text":"jugaadlang.errors.messages class JugaadError(Exception) \u2014 Base class for compiler/runtime errors. class JugaadSyntaxError(JugaadError) \u2014 Syntax errors. class JugaadRuntimeError(JugaadError) \u2014 Runtime errors. class JugaadNameError(JugaadRuntimeError) \u2014 Name errors. class JugaadTypeError(JugaadRuntimeError) \u2014 Type errors. class JugaadZeroDivisionError(JugaadRuntimeError) \u2014 Division by zero. Functions: Function Description format_error(exc, source, filename) Format any exception with funny Hindi message format_syntax_error(msg, line, col, source_line, filename) Format syntax errors with caret highlighting FUNNY_ERRORS dict \u2014 Maps Python exception type names to humorous Hindi titles and descriptions."},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.repl","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangrepl","text":"Module: jugaadlang.repl"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.repl.repl","url":"api.html#jugaadlangreplrepl","text":"jugaadlang.repl.repl class JugaadREPL Method Description JugaadREPL() Init with persistent interpreter and history .start() Launch interactive REPL loop Uses prompt_toolkit.PromptSession with: - PygmentsLexer(JugaadPygmentsLexer) \u2014 Syntax highlighting - WordCompleter(KEYWORDS_LIST) \u2014 Auto-completion - FileHistory \u2014 Persistent history - AutoSuggestFromHistory() \u2014 Suggestion"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"Module: jugaadlang.package_manager","url":"api.html#module-jugaadlangpackage_manager","text":"Module: jugaadlang.package_manager"},{"title":"Internal API","heading":"jugaadlang.package_manager.manager","url":"api.html#jugaadlangpackage_managermanager","text":"jugaadlang.package_manager.manager class JugaadPackageManager All methods are static: Method Description JugaadPackageManager.install(package) Install package/bundle via pip JugaadPackageManager.remove(package) Uninstall package JugaadPackageManager.update(package) Upgrade package JugaadPackageManager.search(query) Search PyPI and stdlib PACKAGE_MAP \u2014 Bundle definitions mapping short aliases to pip packages."}];
